1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:02,210
RADIO: ...population centers first...

2
00:00:02,800 --> 00:00:04,200
PREVIOUSLY: DAY 1 · NIGHT

3
00:00:04,320 --> 00:00:08,980
A fire. A missing man. Three blinks from a roof.

4
00:00:09,760 --> 00:00:14,540
First light, Day 2. Three buddies. One rope.

5
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:16,620
[WES PRUITT] WES: Cal! CAL!

6
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:18,730
[CAL PRUITT · Wes's twin] CAL: Took you long enough.

7
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:22,350
CAL: Ankle's gone. Rest of me's fine.

8
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:25,760
WES: Rope on. Nobody unclips.

9
00:00:29,800 --> 00:00:34,220
DRIZZLE: Good news: he's alive. Bad news: he's heavy.

10
00:00:37,400 --> 00:00:42,440
Three days. No helicopter. But the camp had a toilet.

11
00:00:44,800 --> 00:00:49,400
Two hundred twelve people. Every one of them with a job.

12
00:00:50,600 --> 00:00:52,230
[MS. ORTEGA · the teacher] MS. ORTEGA: Line up by twos!

13
00:00:52,400 --> 00:00:55,820
MS. ORTEGA: Buddy's name, out loud. Adults too.

14
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:59,660
DRIZZLE: Drizzle! My buddy is... Mags.

15
00:01:00,200 --> 00:01:01,620
MAGS: Lucky me.

16
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:06,520
[GORD PIKE] GORD: Folks! Shifts are on the board.

17
00:01:06,640 --> 00:01:11,280
GORD: Water, wood, latrine, watch. Sign up.

18
00:01:11,400 --> 00:01:13,980
DRIZZLE: Latrine. Somebody has to.

19
00:01:14,100 --> 00:01:16,930
GORD: And what you've got goes on my list too.

20
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:22,200
[BENNY OCHOA] BENNY: Stove stays outside. Learned that one.

21
00:01:22,320 --> 00:01:25,580
BENNY: Rolling boil. One full minute.

22
00:01:26,200 --> 00:01:27,470
DRIZZLE: And the timer?

23
00:01:28,600 --> 00:01:30,510
BENNY: Nothing else to do up here.

24
00:01:31,800 --> 00:01:36,200
BOIL: A ROLLING BOIL FOR 1 FULL MINUTE

25
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:40,390
MAGS: Clear water, no fuel? Bleach.

26
00:01:40,510 --> 00:01:44,360
MAGS: Unscented. The label tells you how many drops.

27
00:01:44,480 --> 00:01:45,950
DRIZZLE: Then we drink?

28
00:01:46,070 --> 00:01:49,240
MAGS: Stir. Then wait thirty minutes.

29
00:01:49,360 --> 00:01:54,540
BLEACH: UNSCENTED ONLY · DROPS PER LABEL · WAIT 30 MIN

30
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:58,100
[DANA REYES · first aid] DANA: Sit. Foot up. Don't look.

31
00:01:58,220 --> 00:01:59,790
CAL: Wasn't gonna look.

32
00:02:00,600 --> 00:02:02,610
DRIZZLE: Here. The whole kit.

33
00:02:03,400 --> 00:02:05,280
DANA: Gord gave your bag back?

34
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:07,550
DRIZZLE: He "found" it.

35
00:02:08,400 --> 00:02:11,600
DRIZZLE: It's not a snack bag anymore. It's the camp's.

36
00:02:16,200 --> 00:02:17,860
[MILO VARGA] MILO: Mom. Tell him.

37
00:02:19,800 --> 00:02:22,020
[TESS VARGA] TESS: Drizzle. Not here.

38
00:02:23,200 --> 00:02:25,400
TESS: Come with me. Alone.

39
00:02:31,200 --> 00:02:33,490
TESS: Insulin. Milo's.

40
00:02:35,200 --> 00:02:36,830
DRIZZLE: Does it need a fridge?

41
00:02:37,800 --> 00:02:40,270
TESS: It lasts a few weeks out of one.

42
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:44,400
TESS: If they know, they'll want it.

43
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:48,800
DRIZZLE: Then nobody knows. Promise.

44
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:56,250
MAGS: Downhill. Well away from the water.

45
00:02:56,600 --> 00:02:59,170
DRIZZLE: Seventy-one. Seventy-two.

46
00:02:59,600 --> 00:03:02,430
MAGS: Two hundred feet. Then dig.

47
00:03:03,600 --> 00:03:12,000
LATRINE: 200 FT / 60 M FROM WATER AND CAMP, DOWNHILL

48
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:18,410
DRIZZLE: Good news: I'm still waterproof. Bad news: so is the latrine.

49
00:03:18,530 --> 00:03:22,660
MAGS: Soap after. Every time. Everyone.

50
00:03:22,780 --> 00:03:28,540
WASH HANDS WITH SOAP AFTER EVERY USE

51
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:31,710
WES: Rope it off. Nobody washes here.

52
00:03:32,200 --> 00:03:35,020
CAL: Drinking only. Sign says so.

53
00:03:35,140 --> 00:03:40,740
MARK AND PROTECT THE WATER SOURCE

54
00:03:43,400 --> 00:03:45,090
RADIO: ...this is the emergency...

55
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:50,910
RADIO: ...relief prioritized... for population centers...

56
00:03:51,600 --> 00:03:54,800
RADIO: ...smaller coastal communities... to follow...

57
00:03:55,800 --> 00:03:58,130
[DARLA FINCH] DARLA: To follow? Follow when?

58
00:03:59,600 --> 00:04:01,460
GORD: Folks. We're fine.

59
00:04:02,600 --> 00:04:05,200
GORD: We have a plan. We have a list.

60
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:12,610
In most disasters, people help each other first.

61
00:04:13,800 --> 00:04:17,090
DRIZZLE: Boil one minute. Latrine downhill.

62
00:04:17,600 --> 00:04:20,740
MAGS: Soap. And everybody gets a job.

63
00:04:21,200 --> 00:04:22,160
MILO: Even me?

64
00:04:23,200 --> 00:04:26,260
DRIZZLE: Especially you. Head of flashlights.

65
00:04:31,200 --> 00:04:34,260
That night, the list of who had what...

66
00:04:39,600 --> 00:04:41,460
...went into Gord's tent.
